<%#
  The whole thread, replaced.

  Answering appends, so it streams only the tail. Going back does the opposite —
  a row disappears and an earlier step reopens — and there is no honest way to
  express a shrink as an append. Replacing the list outright is correct by
  construction and cheap: rows are one line of markup each, and Back is a
  deliberate, occasional act rather than the every-step path.

  locals: as runner/_thread
%>
<%= turbo_stream.replace "runner-thread" do %>
  <%= render "runner/thread",
        scenario: scenario, step: step, next_url: next_url, stop_url: stop_url,
        back_button: back_button, show_cancel: show_cancel,
        errors: errors, submitted: submitted, auto_advance: auto_advance,
        parked: parked, results_url: results_url %>
<% end %>
